            "Henry Edward \"Ed\" Roberts",
            "(September 13, 1941 -April 1, 2010)",
            "was an American engineer, entrepreneur and",
            "medical doctor who invented the first",
            "commercially successful personal computer in",
            "1975. He is most often known as \"the father of",
            "the personal computer\". The computer was",
            "available as a kit for $439 or assembled for",
            "$621 and had several additional add-ons such",
            "as a memory board and interface boards. By",
            "August 1975, over 5,000 Altair 8800 personal",
            "computers were sold; starting the personal",
            "computer revolution."
          ]
        },
